{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCurrent recovery handles interrupted creates but not the retired-first/live-replace crash state where one exact identity remains both live and tombstoned. Recovery must never guess across mismatched identities.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract create recovery and add a pure interrupted-retirement classifier plus repository-backed completion operation behind the `BindingStore` facade. Do not invoke it automatically yet.\n\n## Plan\n1. Move keyed/keyless create recovery into `binding_recovery.py` without changing labels, immutable known-key behavior, three-miss plus 3600-second grace, failure tally, or continue behavior. Keep the facade's `recover_pending_bindings` signature and return value so the existing `run_differs.py` call site is untouched.\n2. Build real fault-cut fixtures for a tombstone persisted before live replacement fails.\n3. Classify retirement completion only when the tombstone, the live forward entry, and the live reverse entry agree on exact local id and Jira key.\n4. Complete by removing the redundant live forward/reverse pair while retaining the tombstone; repeat is a no-op. Mismatch, corruption, or replace failure safety-aborts and retains evidence.\n\n## Testing\nUse fresh store reloads, identity-mismatch tables, replacement cuts, and keyed/keyless create-recovery regressions. The existing create-recovery suites (`test_write_ahead_recovery.py`, `test_recovery_loud_failures.py`, `test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py`, `test_identity_write_retention_heldout.py`) are the extraction's regression oracle and must pass unmodified; new tests add a direct-module tier rather than duplicating them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exact tombstone/forward/reverse overlap completes to coherent retired-only bytes while retaining the tombstone.\n- [ ] Repeating completion performs no write.\n- [ ] Any identity mismatch, corrupt live file, or replace failure retains evidence and returns a typed safety abort.\n- [ ] Keyed pending recovery performs no search.\n- [ ] Keyless pending recovery still requires both three misses and 3600 seconds, and one entry failure does not stop others.\n- [ ] The pre-existing create-recovery invocation gate is behaviorally unchanged by this move: it stays scoped-passes-only with no write-bearing gate, and no new write-bearing or scope condition is attached to it.\n\n## Out of scope\nAutomatic invocation boundary for retirement completion, rich-emission caller cutover, and ADR finalization."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787135468839241001,"uuid":"93a67061-edc1-462a-93a2-562da6d2b10d"}